  "businessRules": [
    "Customer email and name are required fields for customer creation",
    "Product name and price are required fields for product creation",
    "Orders are created with status DRAFT by default",
    "Orders require a customerId and at least one item (productId + quantity) to be created",
    "When an order is created, a DRAFT entry is immediately added to OrderStatusHistory - observed sequence after creation: [DRAFT]",
    "When an order status changes from DRAFT to SUBMITTED, a new SUBMITTED entry is added to OrderStatusHistory - observed sequence after submit: [DRAFT, SUBMITTED]",
    "SUBMITTED orders cannot be edited, deleted, or reverted to DRAFT (Submit, Edit, Delete buttons disappear from UI)",
    "Only DRAFT orders have Submit, Edit, and Delete actions available in the UI",
    "Order status can only be DRAFT or SUBMITTED (enum constraint in API)",
    "OrderItem unitPrice is captured at order creation time (snapshotted from product price)",
    "Kafka events are published to orders.status-changed topic when order status changes (both initial DRAFT on creation and subsequent status updates)",
    "The root URL '/' redirects to '/customers'",
    "Order status history is viewable via 'Show history' toggle in the UI"
  ],
